      "title": "Je m'appelle...",
      "description": "Introduce yourself and ask people their name.",
      "estimatedMinutes": 12,
      "sections": [
        {
          "type": "learn",
          "title": "Learn",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "heading": "Saying your name",
              "body": "To say your name, French uses \"je m'appelle\" — literally \"I call myself\". To ask someone's name, say \"Comment tu t'appelles ?\" to a friend, or \"Comment vous appelez-vous ?\" in polite situations.",
              "examples": [
                { "french": "Je m'appelle Marie.", "english": "My name is Marie." },
                { "french": "Comment tu t'appelles ?", "english": "What's your name? (informal)" },
                { "french": "Comment vous appelez-vous ?", "english": "What is your name? (formal)" },
                { "french": "Je me présente : Léa Martin.", "english": "Let me introduce myself: Léa Martin." },
                { "french": "Et toi, comment tu t'appelles ?", "english": "And you, what's your name?" }
              ],
              "tip": "Notice the elision: \"me appelle\" becomes \"m'appelle\" — French drops the e before a vowel."
            },
            {
              "heading": "Nice to meet you",
              "body": "After hearing someone's name, say \"Enchanté !\" (delighted!). A woman writes \"Enchantée\" with an extra e — it sounds exactly the same. With friends, you can also introduce yourself casually with \"Moi, c'est Paul.\"",
              "examples": [
                { "french": "Enchanté !", "english": "Nice to meet you! (said by a man)" },
                { "french": "Enchantée !", "english": "Nice to meet you! (said by a woman)" },
                { "french": "Moi, c'est Paul.", "english": "I'm Paul. (casual)" },
                { "french": "Voici mon amie Sarah.", "english": "This is my friend Sarah." },
                { "french": "Qui est-ce ? — C'est Paul.", "english": "Who is it? — It's Paul." }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
